<title>POLAND: PBR leads consortium to lend $27 mln.</title>
<headline>PBR leads consortium to lend $27 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A consortiumn of four banks led by the Polish Development Bank (PBR) has concluded an agreement to lend the Gdynia shipyard $27.1 million to build a container ship, PBR said in a statement.</p>
<p>PBR said other banks in the consortium were Bank Zachodni SA, Bank Przemyslowo-Handlowy (BPH) and Powszechny Bank Kredytowy SA (PBK).</p>
<p>PBR said its share of the loan would be $3.6 million.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
